===Etymology===
{{multiple images
|direction = vertical
|image1 = Crescentia cujete WS.JPG
|caption1 = The calabash or [[calabash tree]] (''[[Crescentia cujete]]''; ''sense 1'') and its fruit
|image2 = Bầu nậm.jpg
|caption2 = The calabash, [[calabash vine]], or [[bottle gourd]] (''[[Lagenaria siceraria]]''; ''sense 2'') and its fruit
|image3 = Jalpa de Méndez Artesanías.jpg
|caption3 = Calabashes ''(sense 3)'', [[container]]s made from fruits of the calabash tree, from [[Tabasco]], [[Mexico]]
|image4 = Hula calabash.jpg
|caption4 = An [[ipu]], a [[Hawaiian#Adjective|Hawaiian]] calabash ''(sense 5)'' often used to provide a [[beat#Noun|beat]] for [[hula]] [[dancing#Noun|dancing]]. It is made from two fruit of the calabash vine joined together
}}

From {{der|en|fr|calebasse}}, from {{der|en|es|calabaza||gourd; pumpkin}}, possibly from {{der|en|ar|[[قرع|قَرْعَةٌ]] [[يابس|يَابِسَةٌ]]|t=dry gourd}} or directly from its {{glossary|etymon}} {{der|en|fa|خربزه|tr=xarboze|t=melon}},<ref name="OED">{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=26129|date=1888}}</ref><ref>{{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref> possibly ultimately from {{der|en|sa|त्रपुस||colocynth fruit}} (compare {{noncog|fa|تربز|تربزه|tr=tarboze|t=watermelon}}). The English word is cognate with {{cog|ca|carabassa|t=pumpkin; orange colour}}, {{cog|gl|cabaza|t=gourd, pumpkin, squash; calabash (container)}}, {{cog|oc|calebasso}}, {{m|oc|carabasso}}, {{m|oc|carbasso}}, {{cog|pt|cabaça|t=gourd; calabash (container)}}, {{cog|scn|caravazza}}.<ref name="OED"/>

